      "writtenOn": "2024-07-08T10:19:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the conversion between int[] and ArrayList\u003cInteger\u003e would cause boxing of a bunch of extra objects that will then need to be GCed, for each NRI and every time CS needs to send a callback. It\u0027s hard to estimate whether it would make a big difference but to be safe I\u0027d rather work with the int[] directly.\n\nAdded a GrowingIntArray class as suggested in another comment; that class would likely be useful in other situations too, and using it should be about as easy as using ArrayList\u003cInteger\u003e. Added a bit more details on the memory and garbage collection in the GrowingIntArray javadoc.",
      "parentUuid": "fddd3f24_c8afa2a4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 30,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 30,
        "endChar": 31
